-- CK-106: a `number` receiver's method inside a recursive binding group is
-- `unknown_method` at the use, in every declaration order (checker-v2.md
-- §10.8, R7's round-2 review, S3). `mb` passes the literal `3` for `ma`'s
-- `x`, so `x` is a `number` never chosen between `Int` and `Float`, and
-- nothing can answer `x.size ()`: outside a group the caller reports that
-- (`unknown_method` at the instantiation); inside one, `mb`'s call is a
-- group call and §12.3's case 3 has no structural answer for `size`. Before
-- the fix v2 reported two `internal`s at `ma 0 3` (case 3, then I7); v1
-- reports an `internal` I7 at `x.size ()`.
ma n x =
    if n > 0 then
        mb n

    else
        x.size ()


mb n =
    ma 0 3
